JAVA ?? why created ???
ANS :--> created by james gosling in the year 1995 (sun microsystem) inorder to solve the biggest software development issue i.e. inability to exceute same program on multiple machines beacuse all machine dont hve same hardware or same operating system inoredr to solve he created java WORA
WRITE ONCE RUN ANYWHERE ( Provided ability to execute the program on all machines irrespective of thier OS)

JAVA is high level , object oriented , secure , robust , platform independent , WORA , Architecture neutral , Multithreaded , Exception handling
, distributed , Automatic garbage collection

JDK ---> JRE + JVM + Other Development tools( JDB - debugger , JAVAC - compiler ,jdoc - documentation , jar)
JRE ----> It's a package that contains JVM + JAVA Libraries , it provides runtime env to run java code
JVM ---> It executes the byte code , dont care about .java file , it only care about .class file (Bytecode)
Responsibilities of the JVM:
Loads classes   ---> Classloader loads the class files into JVM , Without this JVM wont be able to know where are the classes exists
Verifies bytecode ---> Bytecode Verifier (Before execution JVM checks (Is it valid , any corrupt data )
Manages memory
Runs garbage collection
Executes code ---> After bytecode verification JVM executes the program convert it into native machine code
Provides security


